   "source": [
    "**Empirical P90 validates the parametric assumption at annual resolution.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Comparing the parametric P90 (normal-distribution, `mean - 1.282*std`) against\n",
    "the empirical 10th percentile of each district's 19-year annual series: only\n",
    "5 of 77 districts (6.5%) show empirical P90 below parametric, and the largest\n",
    "gap is -0.33% (Salyan). The average gap across all 77 districts is +0.67%,\n",
    "meaning empirical P90 is on average slightly *higher* than parametric, not\n",
    "lower. At annual resolution, the normal-distribution assumption does not\n",
    "understate tail risk in this dataset. This does not extend to monsoon-season resolution, where inter-annual CoV runs 10-20% (see Chart 6) rather than the 2-4% annual CoV this comparison is based on. A heavier-tailed monthly distribution would not necessarily be visible in this annual-level check, and the monsoon P90/P50 chart (Chart 5b) should be read with that gap in mind."
   ]
