   "source": [
    "Scenario A was tested across a NPR 80-85M/MW CAPEX range, reflecting the cost band typically observed for 10 MW utility-scale solar in Nepal during the generation-1 period. The two endpoints produce materially different covenant outcomes. At NPR 80M/MW, the project clears the 1.20x covenant across all three years and all three resource cases, with the thinnest margin at Year 10 under worst-year resource (1.201x). At NPR 85M/MW, the same project breaches covenant under worst-year resource at Year 1 (1.182x), and falls below covenant under all resource cases by Year 10 as degradation compounds. A five-million-rupee-per-MW difference in capital cost is the difference between a structurally sound financing position and one with no resource buffer at all. This indicates that covenant compliance for generation-1 projects was not determined by tariff or resource conditions alone, but sat close enough to the threshold that a relatively narrow range in capital cost assumptions determines whether the project is resilient or fragile."
   ]
