   "source": [
    "Scenario B models projects financed under competitive tariff bidding, using a CAPEX of NPR 75M/MW and a 75% debt, 15-year term structure, consistent with the debt ratio used in Scenario A. At the base tariff of NPR 5.94/kWh, the project clears the 1.20x covenant under P50 and trough-average resource through Year 5, but breaches under worst-year resource from project start (1.193x) and falls marginally below covenant under every resource case, including P50, by Year 10 (1.197x) as degradation compounds. Every tariff below the base rate is below covenant from Year 1 under all three resource cases. NPR 5.00/kWh, the lowest tariff tested, is already in default-risk territory at Year 1 under worst-year resource (0.975x) and remains in default-risk territory across all resource cases by Year 10. At this leverage, competitively bid tariffs at or below NPR 5.55/kWh carry essentially no resource buffer, and the thinnest coverage in every tariff tier corresponds to the documented 2015-2021 trough or its associated worst years."
   ]
