    "## Phase 2d: Extended Resource Risk Testing\n",
    "Recomputes trough exposure against a pre-trough baseline, extends the DSCR\n",
    "stress test to monthly and quarterly resolution, screens for bifacial\n",
    "relevance, and statistically tests the 2015-2021 trough against random chance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7dd0982-1f5f-4dc3-bff9-7ad464486e13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Trough Risk on a Pre-Trough Baseline\n",
    "Recomputes trough duration risk tiers using the 2005-2014 average as the threshold denominator, in place of the 19-year mean used in Phase 2b. The 19-year mean incorporates the trough years it is being tested against, which understates underperformance. A pretrough baseline produces a stricter threshold. The base and downside resource scenario split does not need recomputing here: the window-overlap problem was resolved by moving the base case to the non-overlapping 2022-2023 period in the Forward Resource Scenarios cell above.\n",
    "\n",
    "This substitutes for the 3-year rolling baseline (2005-2007) sensitivity test noted as planned in the Phase 1 Limitations section; a 2005-2014 pre-trough baseline was used instead because it directly stress-tests the trough-duration risk-tier threshold, the metric most sensitive to baseline choice, rather than re-testing the endpoint comparison itself."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "e0195a67-13bf-4b89-9323-f80d9a89cb44",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trough risk tiers, pre-trough (2005-2014) baseline vs original (19-year mean) baseline:\n",
      "risk_tier\n",
      "Low    77\n",
      "\n",
      "Districts with 5+ consecutive years below 95% of pre-trough baseline:\n",
      "Empty DataFrame\n",
      "Columns: [district, zone, max_consecutive]\n",
      "Index: []\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ================================================================\n",
    "# PRE-TROUGH BASELINE CORRECTION\n",
    "# Both the trough risk tiers and the base/downside scenario split\n",
    "# were computed against the 19-year mean, which already includes\n",
    "# the trough years it's measuring against. This recomputes both\n",
    "# using a 2005-2014 pre-trough baseline instead.\n",
    "# ================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "pretrough_mean = (df_yearly_trend_77[df_yearly_trend_77['year'] <= 2014]\n",
    "                   .groupby('location')['GHI_annual'].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "trough_data_corrected = []\n",
    "for location in df_yearly_trend_77['location'].unique():\n",
    "    df_loc = df_yearly_trend_77[df_yearly_trend_77['location'] == location].copy()\n",
    "    zone = df_loc['zone'].values[0]\n",
    "    baseline = pretrough_mean[location]\n",
    "    threshold = baseline * 0.95\n",
    "    df_loc['below_threshold'] = df_loc['GHI_annual'] < threshold\n",
    "    years_below = df_loc['below_threshold'].sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "    max_run, current = 0, 0\n",
    "    for v in df_loc.sort_values('year')['below_threshold']:\n",
    "        if v: current += 1; max_run = max(max_run, current)\n",
    "        else: current = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "    risk_tier = \"High\" if max_run >= 5 else (\"Moderate\" if max_run >= 3 else \"Low\")\n",
    "    trough_data_corrected.append({'district': location, 'zone': zone,\n",
    "                                   'pretrough_baseline': round(baseline, 1),\n",
    "                                   'years_below_95pct': int(years_below),\n",
    "                                   'max_consecutive': int(max_run), 'risk_tier': risk_tier})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_trough_corrected = pd.DataFrame(trough_data_corrected).sort_values(\n",
