    "**Interpreting the null result above**\n",
    "\n",
    "Neither baseline (the original 19-year mean, nor the stricter pre-trough\n",
    "2005-2014 baseline) classifies any of the 77 districts as Moderate or High\n",
    "risk under the 5-consecutive-year threshold. This does not contradict the\n",
    "system-wide trough finding confirmed later in this section by bootstrap\n",
    "resampling (5.6% average depth, 95% CI -7.1% to -4.3%) and by a\n",
    "permutation test on run length (p=0.049). Average pairwise inter-district\n",
    "GHI anomaly correlation is 0.824, meaning districts move together\n",
    "directionally but not in lockstep: a threshold requiring 95%-of-baseline\n",
    "performance for 5 straight years at a single district is a stricter bar\n",
    "than the system-wide average trough depth would suggest, because\n",
    "individual-year noise at the district level occasionally interrupts an\n",
    "otherwise persistent system-wide pattern. Read this as a limitation of a\n",
    "per-district threshold test applied to a system-wide phenomenon, not as\n",
    "evidence against the trough itself. A lender assessing an individual\n",
    "project should rely on the system-wide bootstrap and DSCR results in this\n",
    "notebook, not on this risk-tier classification, for trough exposure."
