    "### Monthly and Quarterly Minimum-DSCR Stress Test\n",
    "Breaks the annual DSCR result down by month and quarter, to find the weakest\n",
    "point in the year rather than just the weakest year.\n",
    "\n",
    "This test is run at NPR 5.94/kWh, Scenario B's base tariff, same CAPEX and\n",
    "debt terms as Scenario B (75M/MW, 75% debt, 15-year term). This tariff clears\n",
    "the 1.20x annual covenant under P50 resource in Year 1 (1.252x, per the\n",
    "Scenario B table above), so any sub-covenant months shown below are not a\n",
    "restatement of a tariff-level shortfall. They isolate a separate risk:\n",
    "whether a level monthly debt-service schedule survives Nepal's seasonal\n",
    "generation profile even when the annual figure clears covenant.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Read this as a test of intra-year cash flow timing, not a claim that the\n",
    "project defaults monthly.** The model below assumes level monthly debt\n",
    "service (ANNUAL_DS / 12) with no debt service reserve account (DSRA) and\n",
    "no working capital buffer, which is not how real project financing is\n",
    "structured. Actual debt service is typically semi-annual or annual, and\n",
    "projects size a DSRA specifically to bridge low-generation months against\n",
    "high-generation surplus within the year. The result below should inform\n",
    "DSRA sizing in a real term sheet, not be read as a standalone default\n",
    "indicator."
   ]
  },
