    "**Why duration, not depth, is the basis for this analysis**\n",
    "\n",
    "Shorter, sharper single-year dips also occurred within the 2005-2023\n",
    "record (notably 2007-2008 and 2011), in some cases approaching the average\n",
    "depth of the 2015-2021 trough in a single year. These are not treated as\n",
    "equivalent risks here: a single weak year is a shortfall a reserve account\n",
    "or P50 averaging effect can absorb, while a sustained multi-year run\n",
    "erodes debt service coverage across consecutive periods without an\n",
    "intervening recovery year. The run-enumeration table above confirms the\n",
    "2015-2022 window is the clear outlier for duration (8 years, versus a\n",
    "2-year second-longest run), which is why this analysis is structured\n",
    "around the longest sustained run rather than the single worst year."
   ]
