  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "436a4a1b-57a0-4b88-a494-f31049bed18c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reconciling the two significance tests above**\n",
    "\n",
    "Two different tests were run on the same 19-year annual series and they\n",
    "point in different directions. The Wald-Wolfowitz runs test, which counts\n",
    "the total number of above/below-mean runs across the full series, finds\n",
    "9 observed runs against 9.8 expected (p=0.668). Not distinguishable from\n",
    "random ordering. The permutation test, which targets the single longest\n",
    "run specifically (10,000 random shuffles of the same 19 values), finds\n",
    "that a run of 8 or more consecutive below-mean years occurs by chance\n",
    "only 4.9% of the time (p=0.049), a result usually read as significant at\n",
    "the conventional 0.05 threshold. Lag-1 autocorrelation (0.121) is weak.\n",
    "\n",
    "These results are not contradictory in a technical sense. They test\n",
    "different features of the same series, but should not be selectively\n",
    "quoted. The overall pattern of the 19-year series is not\n",
    "distinguishable from random year-to-year noise, but the single longest\n",
    "run in that series (8 consecutive years) is longer than random chance\n",
    "would typically produce. The honest summary is that persistence evidence\n",
    "is present but marginal, not strong, and any external framing of the\n",
    "trough as \"statistically confirmed\" should cite both tests together, not\n",
    "the permutation result alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note on trough length:** the permutation test measures an 8-year\n",
    "longest run, one year longer than the \"2015-2021\" (7-year) window cited\n",
    "in the Financing Implication and DSCR resource-case sections of this\n",
    "notebook. This reflects the test operating on years below the full\n",
    "19-year mean, rather than the 2015-2021 window defined by proximity to\n",
    "the 2005 baseline. Both are legitimate but distinct definitions of\n",
    "\"trough.\" This notebook uses 2015-2021 as its working trough window\n",
    "throughout the DSCR and financing sections; the 8-year statistical run is\n",
    "reported here as a separate, methodologically distinct result and should\n",
    "not be conflated with the 2015-2021 figure elsewhere in this document."
   ]
  },
