    "## Key Findings: Extended Risk Testing (Phase 2b-2d)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Trough persistence, quantified with uncertainty.** The 2015-2021 system-wide trough averaged 5.6% below the 2005 baseline (95% CI: -7.1% to -4.3%, bootstrap resample, n=2000). This is the all-77-district average; it is not in conflict with Phase 1's 8-13% figure, which describes the hardest-hit Terai and Hill zones specifically rather than the national mean, and the two should not be quoted interchangeably. A permutation test finds an 8-year run this long has roughly\n",
    "a 5% probability of occurring by chance (p=0.049), though a standard runs test\n",
    "on total run count does not reach significance (p=0.668) and lag-1\n",
    "autocorrelation is weak (0.121). The persistence signal is real but marginal,\n",
    "not strong, and should not be overstated to reviewers.\n",
    "\n",
    "**District-level risk scoring has not flagged any district as High or\n",
    "Moderate risk**, under either the original 19-year-mean threshold or a\n",
    "stricter pre-trough (2005-2014) baseline. This does not contradict the\n",
    "system-wide trough finding above: average pairwise inter-district GHI\n",
    "anomaly correlation is 0.824, meaning districts move together but not\n",
    "in lockstep, and a 95%-of-baseline threshold applied per district dilutes\n",
    "a signal that is stronger in the system-wide average. The risk-tier\n",
    "framework as built is better suited to flagging individual outlier\n",
    "districts than to capturing systemic multi-year risk, and should not be\n",
    "read as evidence against the trough finding.\n",
    "\n",
    "**ENSO does not explain the trough at annual resolution.** Correlation\n",
    "between DJF-season ONI and system GHI anomaly is weak and not\n",
    "statistically significant (r=-0.137, p=0.576), and the sign runs opposite\n",
    "to the stated hypothesis. Aerosol loading from the Indo-Gangetic Plain,\n",
    "flagged as untested in Phase 1, remains the open attribution question for\n",
    "Phase 3 MERRA-2 work.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The system-wide DSCR resource basis is defensible but not uniform\n",
    "across districts.** Average pairwise GHI anomaly correlation is 0.824.\n",
    "High Mountain districts (Humla 0.554, Mugu 0.592, Jumla 0.677, Dolpa\n",
    "0.680) and isolated outliers (Jhapa 0.718) correlate materially less with\n",
